                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/4862: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ciudad
                                Trujillo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-07T18:00:00-05:00">September 7, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>164. From Wilson. Convention initialing [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >initialed?</hi>]. Leaving tomorrow morning by the plane. Finley remains at Port
                    au Prince; I proceed Miami arriving Washington by railroad early Tuesday
                    morning. Please notify Mrs. Wilson. [Wilson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
